WEEK–1: Install Apache Kafka on a Single Node
Aim

To install and run Apache Kafka on a single node using Docker.

Requirements
Ubuntu
Docker installed and running
Internet connection
STEP 1: Check Docker

Open Terminal and type:

docker --version

You should get something like:

Docker version 28.x.x

If Docker is not installed, install it first.

Also check:

sudo systemctl start docker

Then:

sudo systemctl status docker

You should see:

active (running)
STEP 2: Download Zookeeper Image

Kafka in your lab material uses Zookeeper.

Run:

docker pull wurstmeister/zookeeper

Wait until the download finishes.

You should see something similar to:

Status: Downloaded newer image for wurstmeister/zookeeper
STEP 3: Download Kafka Image

Run:

docker pull wurstmeister/kafka

Again, wait until it finishes.

These are the two images specified in your Week-1 material.

STEP 4: Start Zookeeper

Run:

docker run -d --name zookeeper -p 2181:2181 wurstmeister/zookeeper
What this does
docker run → creates and starts container
-d → runs in background
--name zookeeper → gives container the name zookeeper
-p 2181:2181 → exposes Zookeeper port

Check it:

docker ps

You should see zookeeper running.

STEP 5: Start Kafka

Now run this as one command:

docker run -d --name kafka -p 9092:9092 --link zookeeper:zookeeper -e KAFKA_ZOOKEEPER_CONNECT=zookeeper:2181 -e KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS=PLAINTEXT://localhost:9092 -e KAFKA_LISTENERS=PLAINTEXT://0.0.0.0:9092 wurstmeister/kafka

This is the Kafka command given in your Week-1 material.

Important

If the long command is difficult to type, use the same command in multiple lines:

docker run -d --name kafka -p 9092:9092 --link zookeeper:zookeeper \
-e KAFKA_ZOOKEEPER_CONNECT=zookeeper:2181 \
-e KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS=PLAINTEXT://localhost:9092 \
-e KAFKA_LISTENERS=PLAINTEXT://0.0.0.0:9092 \
wurstmeister/kafka

Do not remove the \ characters when using multiple lines.

STEP 6: Check Both Containers

Run:

docker ps

You should see something like:

CONTAINER ID   IMAGE                 NAMES
xxxxxx         wurstmeister/kafka   kafka
xxxxxx         wurstmeister/...     zookeeper

If both kafka and zookeeper are listed, your Week-1 setup is running. ✅

STEP 7: Check Kafka Logs

To make sure Kafka started correctly:

docker logs kafka

You will get many lines.

If you want to see only the latest logs:

docker logs --tail 20 kafka

If there is no continuous error, Kafka is generally running.

⭐ VERY IMPORTANT FOR LAB EXAM

You can remember Week-1 as only 4 main commands:

1. Pull Zookeeper
docker pull wurstmeister/zookeeper
2. Pull Kafka
docker pull wurstmeister/kafka
3. Run Zookeeper
docker run -d --name zookeeper -p 2181:2181 wurstmeister/zookeeper
4. Run Kafka
docker run -d --name kafka -p 9092:9092 --link zookeeper:zookeeper -e KAFKA_ZOOKEEPER_CONNECT=zookeeper:2181 -e KAFKA_ADVERTISED_LISTENERS=PLAINTEXT://localhost:9092 -e KAFKA_LISTENERS=PLAINTEXT://0.0.0.0:9092 wurstmeister/kafka

Then:

docker ps

If both containers are running → Week-1 completed. ✅

⚠️ If You Get "Container Name Already in Use"

This can happen if you already ran the commands once.

Check:

docker ps -a

If kafka or zookeeper already exists, remove them:

docker rm -f kafka zookeeper

Then start again from STEP 3.

⚠️ If You Get "Cannot Connect to Docker Daemon"

Run:

sudo systemctl start docker

Then retry the commands.

